@@ -145,6 +145,7 @@ before evaluating a candidate built from that cache.
 | 0939 | `kernelbase`: the crash report (0912, 0924) names a C++ exception a program threw and didn't catch (0xe06d7363): its type as the compiler names it and, for a `std::exception`, its message; and it shows the flags register and the 16 bytes of code at the fault. Call of Juarez Gunslinger's engine gave up with an uncaught C++ exception in every log, none saying why; Far Cry's CrySystem.dll faulted on an instruction reported only as a read of FFFFFFFF. Both are read under an exception handler and only add lines to the report |
 | 0940 | `ntdll`: a folder a program makes (or opens if there) as a folder, by its full name, under `C:\users\<name>\`, whose parent isn't there, gets its missing parents made first, as the program's installer would have made them on Windows: a game copied from a PC was never installed here. Call of Juarez Gunslinger's engine makes `AppData\Local\Techland\COJGunslinger`, whose `Techland` its installer makes, and stopped with an uncaught C++ exception when that failed. The users folder and a user's own folder are never made; each parent made is logged |
 | 0941 | `ntdll`: a general protection fault with the nested-task flag (NT, 0x4000) set in the frame clears it and runs the instruction again, logged the first time. A program that sets NT with `popf` (Far Cry's CPU check in CrySystem.dll) made the next `iretq` back to it fault, from Wine's 64-bit side or the kernel's, reported as a read of FFFFFFFF (Wine bug 33275; Linux and Windows clear NT on entry). No program uses NT, and no fault without it changes |
+| 0942 | `win32u`: input event 6 turns the mouse wheel, `x` notches away from the player positive (`MOUSEEVENTF_WHEEL` of `x` times `WHEEL_DELTA`): a USB mouse's wheel, or a controller button bound to `mouse_wheel_up` or `mouse_wheel_down`. Before, the title read a USB mouse's wheel and dropped it, and a button couldn't turn it |
 | 0972 | `faudio` (Wine's bundled FAudio 26.09): upstream FAudio a3b49d6 and 2ead980 (2026-09-26). A source voice that played at the output rate never advanced `resampleOffset`, so when it started resampling, the tap loops of `FAudio_INTERNAL_MixSource` ran from the stale offset, `toResample - tap_samples` wrapped and the SSE2 resampler wrote far past `resampled_audio`. A game corrupted its process heap and crashed in the mixer, or in the heap. FAudio is a static library, so every `xaudio2_*` and `xactengine*` module is in `PE_MODULES` |
 
